<h1>#{title}

<h2 #changes-at-launch>Changes at Launch

<h3 #career>Career
<ul>
  <li>
    Reanimated#{Reanimated} characters are purchased with DNA, which is obtained from:
    <ul>
      <li>Winning, with higher bonuses at higher win streaks.
      <li>Losing, although not as much.
      <li>First game of the day.
      <li>First win of the day.
      <li>Participating in wars.
      <li>Defeating A.I. boss challenges. (unimplemented)
  <li>
    In addition to requiring victories with specific characters, missions also require completing specific objectives, such as killing some number of enemies with a certain skill. Missions no longer depend on rank.

<h3 #mechanics>Mechanics
<ul>
  <li>
    Skills that negate harmful effects, such as ^{Link.skill "Sakura Haruno" Original "Inner Sakura"}, no longer exclude chakra cost changes.
  <li>
    Skills that sacrifice the user's health, such as ^{Link.skill "Rock Lee" Original "Fifth Gate Opening"} and ^{Link.skill "Karin" Shippuden "Heal Bite"}, are treated as a direct loss of health rather than self-directed affliction damage.
  <li>
    New mechanic: destructible barrier, a counterpart to destructible defense. Destructible barrier is a negative effect that absorbs some amount of outgoing damage. It is represented by a red bar next to the health bar, after the blue destructible defense bar.
  <li>
    Several classes have been added for clarity:
    <ul>
      <li><i>Bypassing</i>: Bypasses invulnerability.
      <li><i>Invisible</i>: Cannot be seen by the enemy team.
      <li><i>Soulbound:</i> Effects end when the user dies.
      <li><i>Uncounterable</i>: Cannot be countered.
      <li><i>Unreflectable</i>: Cannot be reflected.
      <li><i>Unremovable</i>: Effects cannot be cured or removed in any way.
  <li>
    The <i>Affliction</i> class has been renamed to <i>Bane</i> in order to avoid confusion with affliction damage. For example, ^{Link.skill "Shino Aburame" Shippuden "Gigantic Beetle Infestation"}, which does not deal any affliction damage, was classified as <i>Affliction</i>.
  <li>
    A few other skills have also been classified as <i>Bane</i>.
  <li>
    The <i>Unique</i> class has been removed.
  <li>
    In addition to <i>Chakra</i>, <i>Mental</i>, and <i>Physical</i> skills, there are now <i>Summon</i> skills. <i>Summon</i> skills are difficult to stun, but easy to avoid.
  <li>
    The <i>Instant</i>, <i>Action</i>, and <i>Control</i> classes have been moved to a new field, Duration, which also indicates how long the skill lasts.
  <li>
    Added the <i>Ongoing</i> duration. <i>Ongoing</i> skills continue to apply their effects even if their user is stunned or otherwise disabled. Examples:
    <ul>
      <li>^{Link.skill "Orochimaru" Original "Major Summoning: Manda"}
      <li>^{Link.skill "Shukaku Gaara" Original "Sand Transformation"}
      <li>^{Link.skill "Tobirama Senju" Reanimated "Water Shockwave"}
      <li>^{Link.skill "Chōji Akimichi" Shippuden "Butterfly Mode"}

<h3 #descriptive-changes>Descriptive Changes
<ul>
  <li>
    Character and skill names use official translations from the anime. For example, Kakashi Hatake's skill "Raikiri" has been renamed to "Lightning Blade".
  <li>
    The term "random chakra" is only used to refer to randomly-generated chakra. The black-colored type of chakra cost is termed "arbitrary chakra" rather than "random chakra", since the user can select any arbitrary chakra to fulfill that cost.
  <li>
    Effects that are stated to last for 1 turn always persist through to the start of the next turn. If an effect does not persist through to the start of the next turn, it is described as lasting "for the rest of the turn", rather than "for 1 turn".

